Long ago, two villages stood on opposite sides of a great river. The Western Village grew abundant grain, while the Eastern Village had none. Each season, the Western Village faced a choice: keep their grain or send it across the river.

The first elder said, "If we send our grain, they will have three times as much. But what if they keep it all?"

